1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,592
Hi, Laura - could you spare a few minutes to talk about the work

2
00:00:02,592 --> 00:00:03,958
placement you did last summer?

3
00:00:03,958 --> 00:00:06,490
I'm thinking of doing one myself.

4
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:08,103
Hi, Tim.

5
00:00:08,103 --> 00:00:08,910
Sure.

6
00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:13,500
Didn't you do yours at an environmental services company?

7
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:14,316
That's right...

8
00:00:14,316 --> 00:00:20,026
It's only a very small company and they needed someone to produce a company

9
00:00:20,026 --> 00:00:20,434
brochure,

10
00:00:20,434 --> 00:00:26,145
and I wanted to get some business experience because l'm interested in a career

11
00:00:26,145 --> 00:00:29,000
in occupational psychology in a business environment.

12
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,130
It was good because I had overall responsibility for the project.

13
00:00:34,130 --> 00:00:38,160
What kind of skills do you think you developed on the placement?

14
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:41,287
I mean, apart from the ones you already had ...

15
00:00:41,287 --> 00:00:45,805
Did you have to do all the artwork for the brochure, the layout

16
00:00:45,805 --> 00:00:46,500
and everything?

17
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:50,450
We hired the services of a professional photographer for that.

18
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:56,000
I did have to use my IT skills to a certain extent because I cut

19
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,220
and pasted text from marketing leaflets,

20
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:01,550
but that didn't involve anything I hadn't done before.

21
00:01:01,550 --> 00:01:06,620
Do you think you got any better at managing your time and prioritising things?

22
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:09,400
You always used to say you had trouble with that ...

23
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:09,835
Oh.

24
00:01:09,835 --> 00:01:10,270
definitely.

25
00:01:10,270 --> 00:01:14,620
There was so much pressure to meet the project deadline.

26
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:19,250
And I also got better at explaining things and asserting my opinions,

27
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:23,495
because I had to have weekly consultations with the marketing manager

28
00:01:23,495 --> 00:01:25,810
and give him a progress report.

29
00:01:25,810 --> 00:01:28,570
It sounds as if you got a lot out of it then.

30
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:29,194
Absolutely.

31
00:01:29,194 --> 00:01:31,691
It was really worthwhile ...

32
00:01:31,691 --> 00:01:36,060
But you know, the company benefited too ...

33
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:38,280
Yes, they must have done.

34
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:43,908
After all, if they'd used a professional advertising agency to produce their brochure instead

35
00:01:43,908 --> 00:01:48,330
of doing it in-house, presumably they'd have paid a lot more?

36
00:01:48,330 --> 00:01:49,305
Oh, yes.

37
00:01:49,305 --> 00:01:54,670
I worked it out - it would have been 250 percent more.

38
00:01:54,670 --> 00:01:59,066
And I thought the end result was good, even though we did everything on

39
00:01:59,066 --> 00:01:59,380
site.

40
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:04,778
The company has quite a powerful computer and I managed to borrow some scanning

41
00:02:04,778 --> 00:02:06,320
software from the university.

42
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:08,820
The new brochure looks really professional;

43
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:12,570
it enhances the image of the company straight away.

44
00:02:12,570 --> 00:02:17,045
So in the long run it should help them to attract clients,

45
00:02:17,045 --> 00:02:18,910
and improve their sales figures?

46
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:20,312
That's the idea.

47
00:02:20,312 --> 00:02:20,780
Yeah.

48
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:26,321
Well, all in all it sounds very positive - I think I will go ahead

49
00:02:26,321 --> 00:02:28,695
and apply for a placement myself.

50
00:02:28,695 --> 00:02:31,070
How do I go about it?

51
00:02:31,070 --> 00:02:33,895
It's easy enough to do,

52
00:02:33,895 --> 00:02:41,240
because there's a government agency called STEP - S-T-E-P - that organises placements for students.

53
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:45,458
You should start by getting their booklet with all the details 一 I expect

54
00:02:45,458 --> 00:02:47,730
you can download one from their website.

55
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:52,066
Actually, they've got copies in the psychology department - I've seen them there.

56
00:02:52,066 --> 00:02:55,680
I'll just go to the office and pick one up.

57
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:56,012
Right.

58
00:02:56,012 --> 00:03:00,660
And then if I were you, after I'd looked at it I'd go over

59
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:02,320
all the options with someone ...

60
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:05,429
I suppose I should ask my tutor's advice.

61
00:03:05,429 --> 00:03:08,150
He knows more about me than anyone.

62
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:12,789
One of the career officers would be better, they've got more knowledge about the

63
00:03:12,789 --> 00:03:15,440
jobs market than your personal tutor would have.

64
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:16,610
OK ...

65
00:03:16,610 --> 00:03:20,575
And then when you know what you want you can register with STEP -

66
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,710
you'll find their address in the booklet.

67
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:28,413
And once you've registered they assign you to a mentor who looks after your

68
00:03:28,413 --> 00:03:28,820
application.

69
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:33,350
And then I suppose you just sit back and wait till you hear something?

70
00:03:33,350 --> 00:03:37,978
They told me at the careers office that it's best to be proactive,

71
00:03:37,978 --> 00:03:42,250
and get updates yourself by checking the website for new placement alerts.

72
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:45,010
Your mentor is supposed to keep you informed,

73
00:03:45,010 --> 00:03:47,080
but you can't rely on that.

74
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:52,224
I don't suppose it，s a good idea to get in touch with companies directly,

75
00:03:52,224 --> 00:03:52,910
is it?

76
00:03:52,910 --> 00:03:53,532
Not really.

77
00:03:53,532 --> 00:03:57,887
But it is the company who notifies you if they want you to go

78
00:03:57,887 --> 00:03:58,820
for an interview.

79
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:03,550
You get a letter of invitation or an email from personnel departments.

80
00:04:03,550 --> 00:04:06,210
And do I reply directly to them?

81
00:04:06,210 --> 00:04:07,196
Yes, you do.

82
00:04:07,196 --> 00:04:11,140
STEP only gets involved again once you've been made a job offer.

83
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:11,548
Right...

84
00:04:11,548 --> 00:04:17,255
So once you've had an interview you should let your mentor know what the

85
00:04:17,255 --> 00:04:18,070
outcome is?

86
00:04:18,070 --> 00:04:20,635
I mean whether you're offered a job,

87
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:23,200
and whether you've decided to accept it?

88
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:23,916
That's right.

89
00:04:23,916 --> 00:04:27,854
They'll inform the careers office once a placement has been agreed,

90
00:04:27,854 --> 00:04:30,360
so you don't have to do that.

91
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:32,440
Is that all then?

92
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:33,610
More or less.

93
00:04:33,610 --> 00:04:38,680
Only once you've accepted an offer you'll pRobably have to supply a reference,

94
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:41,800
because the placement will be conditional on that.

95
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:45,240
And that's something you should ask your own tutor to provide.

96
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:50,880
He knows about your academic ability and also about your qualities, like reliability.

97
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:56,000
Well, thanks very much for the information 一 I'm starting to look forward ...
